--- A value that can fail, dropped by its line — a call made for what it
--- does (`write[path, text]` alone) — is decided on as a read of a failed
--- value is: a function hands the failure back, the top level halts. It had
--- gone by unseen in both modes. Assigned, the failure is a value kept;
--- what a line hands on (a collecting loop's last) is no drop.
kept = write['/nonexistent_dir_for_crow_parity/a.txt', 'hello']
log[kept.ok]
nums = for s in ['1', 'x']
    int[s]
log[nums]
fn save[path]
    write[path, 'hi']
    return 'saved'
r = save['/nonexistent_dir_for_crow_parity/b.txt']
log[r.ok]
log[starts[r.reason, 'cannot write']]
log['next, a write whose failure nothing keeps']
write['/nonexistent_dir_for_crow_parity/c.txt', 'hello']
log['not reached']
